+integrity-clean persistent Triton fallback after same-card CUPTI crossover,
+changed-input A/B/A, and two 19/19 full-suite confirmations.  Its four-row M
+tile removes padded work while shape-proven segment sizes prevent cross-call
+watermark overlap.  The tiny path consumes the same accepted whole-K e4m3
+transform as CuTe through tile-contiguous W13/W2 views; weights never drop
+below e4m3.
+At T=1, every persistent CTA derives the exact current-call route vector in
+registers, avoiding the global histogram/barrier; deterministic output-slice
+initialization and exactly bounded cleanup preserve zero-route and cross-call
+correctness.
+The direct-routing candidate passed two floor-clearing 19/19 full suites at
+2.5599x mean / 2.7047x large and 2.6258x mean / 2.7337x large (CUPTI); an
+additional 19/19 variance sample measured 2.6017x / 2.6840x.
+
+The fused CuTe path differentiates TMA cache residency: one-shot FP8 weight
+tiles use evict_first, while activation tiles reused across expert N-items
+use evict_last.  This changes cache priority only, not data or arithmetic.
+Its GEMM1 producer also issues the second weight stage before waiting for the
+permuted activation tile, then completes both combined barriers with live A
+copies after the acquire gate.  This overlaps useful TMA traffic with routing
+without changing the shared-memory ring, stage count, or numerical path.
+Captured T=14 and T=59 use independent 108- and 112-CTA M64 persistent
+instances; other selected M64 shapes keep the full 148-CTA grid.  Diagnostic
+M128 fallbacks retain the previously proven 108/122/112 grids.
+At T=16 and T=32, the M64 inline activation requantizer column-stripes each
+sparse live row across four and two warps, respectively.  This changes only
+warp ownership of the current call's bf16-to-e4m3 conversion; every column and
+row scale is still rewritten before GEMM2.  All other shapes retain the
+two-row-per-warp mapping.
+The exact-grid follow-up passed two 19/19 full-suite confirmations.
 
 Pipeline per call (3 kernel launches from one compiled host function):
